    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0594" n="582" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24546/38: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Wellington</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cox</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-22T16:00:00-05:00">November 22,
                            1941—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Refer Department’s November 13, 11 p.m.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d575-f1"/> It is
                    Department’s understanding that arrangements being worked out by General Short
                    and Air Commodore Saunders will include through flights to be made by United
                    States service aircraft over New Zealand territory or mandated islands. It is
                    understood that this is agreeable to New Zealand military authorities. Please
                    mention matter in strict confidence to appropriate high officer of New Zealand
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
